<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">First Mexican Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">1821 CE – 1823 CE · capital Mexico City</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived empire of Agustín de Iturbide, the first independent Mexican state, which briefly stretched from California to Costa Rica.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In February 1821 the royalist officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Agustín de Iturbide</a> joined the insurgent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicente-guerrero">Vicente Guerrero</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plan-of-iguala">Plan of Iguala</a>, promising independence, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> and equality under a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a>. The last Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-odonoju">Juan O'Donojú</a>, accepted it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-cordoba">Treaty of Córdoba</a> in August, and the Army of the Three Guarantees entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> on 27 September 1821.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A regency governed while a European prince was sought, but none accepted, and in May 1822 crowds and soldiers acclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Iturbide</a> as Emperor Agustín I. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> joined the empire in January 1822. Iturbide clashed with the congress over money and power and dissolved it in October 1822. The treasury was empty, the army unpaid and the provinces restless.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a> rose at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz-city">Veracruz</a> in December 1822, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plan-of-casa-mata">Plan of Casa Mata</a> in 1823 won over the army. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Iturbide</a> abdicated in March 1823 and went into exile; on his return in 1824 he was executed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> broke away, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-mexican-republic">First Mexican Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/first-mexican-empire.jpg" alt="First Mexican Empire" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Ludovicus Ferdinandus Can have elements by Sodacan and Heralder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_del_Primer_Imperio_Mexicano.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1821 CE – 1823 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mexico City</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Agustín I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a>, <a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, <a href="/countries/el-salvador">El Salvador</a>, <a href="/countries/honduras">Honduras</a>, <a href="/countries/nicaragua">Nicaragua</a>, <a href="/countries/costa-rica">Costa Rica</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mexican Empire (1821-1823), Imperio Mexicano</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1822&amp;focus=first-mexican-empire" aria-label="First Mexican Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2001 1461 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where First Mexican Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2321 1717L2321 1717M2321 1717L2590 1658M2321 1717L2218 1669M2321 1717L2321 1717M2321 1717L2518 1892M2321 1717L2525 1889M2321 1717L2434 1358"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2321 1717h0M2590 1658h0M2218 1669h0M2321 1717h0M2518 